            <ArticleTitle>Adult-acquired flatfoot deformity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>433-439</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00590-017-1945-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adult-acquired flatfoot deformity (AAFD) is a known and recognized cause of pain and disability. Loss of PTT function is the most important contributor to AAFD, and its estimated prevalence is thought to be over 3%. This review aims to summarize the current literature and encompass recent advances regarding AAFD.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
